KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11 --unwind 8
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ padded to the field width: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Meaningful only with the MSVC STL (Windows); elsewhere the #error makes it
fail.  With the MSVC STL, symbolic execution of stream insertion does not
end: cpp11_stream_setw and cpp11_ostream_integer_insertion_classic_locale
time out on VS 2022 and VS 2026 and with --winx64 on MSVC 14.51 headers
preprocessed by cl (5000+ steps through basic_string and the locale
machinery in 60 s, also at --unwind 1).  Not reduced.  Related:
cpp11_standard_stream_objects_initialized_msvc (the locale's runtime
functions have no model).
